WEBVTT

NOTE understand-spatial-adjust: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:06.005
What the feature actually does:
turn the latest moisture scan into

V0-2
00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:09.690
today's percent adjustment, and
write it to Lynx when you push.

V1a-1
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:16.310
It lives inside IntelliDash. Access is
checked per user before the view loads.

V1b-1
00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:19.796
The Spatial Adjust header,
inside IntelliDash.

V2a-1
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:30.309
Each station's Avg. VWC comes from
a TurfRad moisture scan: the average

V2a-2
00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:35.832
volumetric water content measured across
the station, with the date it was captured

V2a-3
00:00:35.932 --> 00:00:41.290
beside the station name. When a station
has no scan, the value is modeled instead.

V2b-1
00:00:41.603 --> 00:00:44.253
Measured moisture and its
scan date, per station.

V3a-1
00:00:49.903 --> 00:00:53.836
Target VWC is the moisture
you want that station to hold.

V3a-2
00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:58.423
It is yours to set, station by
station, between 0 and 50 percent.

V3b-1
00:00:58.936 --> 00:01:03.641
The gap between measured and target
is what the calculation works on.

V3b-2
00:01:03.741 --> 00:01:06.946
Target VWC is an editable
input, not a reading.

V4a-1
00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:16.096
Spatial Adjust turns the
difference between target

V4a-2
00:01:16.196 --> 00:01:19.109
and measured moisture into
a suggested percentage,

V4a-3
00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:22.763
taking today's ET and your
calculation settings into account.

V4b-1
00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.936
The Suggested column is
the output of that chain.

V5a-1
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:34.980
Spatial Adjust never waters anything.
Nothing changes until you push.

V5b-1
00:01:35.543 --> 00:01:38.563
Push Changes is the only thing
that writes to the controller.
